Because the two repositories share an identical dependency stack, the highest-risk false claim here is CROSS-ATTRIBUTION: a fare-related symbol, file, or behaviour attributed to mockb, or a schedule-related symbol, file, or behaviour attributed to mocka. A dependency claim (vitest, typescript) is trivially true in either repository, so it carries no distinguishing power — when the survey cites a dependency as evidence that work belongs to a particular codeline, that is not sufficient grounds on its own. Verify every claim in the repository the survey actually names, not its sibling.

